🧠 Advanced Admiral Maneuvers
1. The "Hammer and Anvil" (Island Pinning)
Since islands block LOS (Line of Sight), you can trap an AI ship.

The Setup: Position your Battleship on one side of a large island and your Destroyer on the other.

The Execution: Use the Destroyer to "flush" the enemy out. The AI will often move away from the Destroyer's torpedo threat, forcing them to sail directly into the Battleship's waiting 10-tile kill zone.

2. The "Sonar Screen" (Defense against Typhoons)
Typhoons reduce your natural vision to almost zero.

The Maneuver: When a Typhoon hits, don't scatter. Move your Destroyer to the center of your fleet formation.

The Benefit: Trigger Sonar Ping. Because Sonar ignores weather degradation, your Destroyer acts as a "Lighthouse," revealing enemies for your Battleships to fire at while they remain safely "blind" to your exact location.

3. "Suppression Chaining"
If you can't sink a ship, neuter it.

The Strategy: A ship is suppressed if it takes >30 damage. If an enemy Battleship is closing in, hit it with a heavy Cruiser or Battleship salvo.

The Result: Even if it survives, its range drops by 25%. This often puts you outside its reach for the next turn, giving you a "free" turn to reposition or fire again without fear of retaliation.

4. "Torpedo Herding"
Torpedoes are slow, but they are scary.

The Strategy: Launch a torpedo North of an enemy ship.

The Result: The AI logic is programmed to avoid the T icons. You can effectively "herd" the enemy into a corner of the map or toward an island where they lose their maneuverability, making them sitting ducks for your Carrier's recon-assisted strikes.

5. "Logistics Cycling" (The 3-2-2 Rotation)
Never have your whole fleet stationary at once.

The Rhythm: Rotate your ships. When your Cruiser is at Tier 2 repair (5 total turns stationary), your Battleship should be aggressive.

The Reset: Once the Cruiser hits 75% HP, move it out immediately. The move resets its repair counter, but it’s better to have a 75% HP ship moving than a 75% HP ship sitting idle and wasting "Combat Tempo."

🌓 Final Pro-Tip: The "Ghost" Snipe
The AI doesn't always move perfectly. If an enemy was at (10, 10) and moved to (11, 11), and then disappeared into the Fog of War, the "Ghost" icons [x] and [+] tell a story.

Calculate the vector: dx=+1,dy=+1.

Aim your next shot at (12, 12).

Blind firing at predicted coordinates is the mark of a Master Admiral in Pacific War 1.
